# Targets removed from the home directory on every `chezmoi apply`.
#
# chezmoi only looks at the current state of the source directory -- it has no
# history, so deleting a `dot_*` file here does NOT delete the file it already
# deployed to existing machines. Listing the target here does.
#
# Entries are permanent while they are listed: anything matching is deleted on
# every apply, so only list paths that must never exist on a managed machine.
# The package half of the same problem lives in the
# `run_onchange_after_*-remove-dependencies.*` scripts.
# See `.docs/dependency-lifecycle.md`.

# `keychain` state directory -- removed in bec4050 (2026-07-23), orphaned when
# Android switched to a fixed agent socket (`~/.ssh/agent.sock`) managed
# directly by `dot_zshrc.tmpl`. The stale `<host>-sh` files here only advertise
# dead random-path sockets.
.keychain

# Cursor -- removed in 601cbeb (2026-07-21), previously managed as dot_cursor/
.cursor

# Gemini CLI -- removed in 601cbeb (2026-07-21)
.gemini

# `claude-local` and `claude-remote` -- removed in #PR_NUMBER (2026-10-15), replaced by
# `claude-omni`, which reaches both GPUs and the cloud providers through OmniRoute.
# `claude-local-task` became `claude-omni-task` in the same change.
.local/bin/claude-local
.local/bin/claude-remote
.local/bin/claude-local-task

# The OmniRoute Compose file -- deployed to ~/local-services by mistake until #PR_NUMBER
# (2026-10-15), which ignores `local-services`: the stack runs from the dotfiles checkout,
# where its `.env` lives, and this copy only drifted from it.
local-services/omniroute/compose.yaml
